## 6. End-to-end data flow

## 6.1 Local-image analysis flow

```text
1. User starts or selects a session.
2. User creates or selects a round.
3. User supplies a local image.
4. Acquisition adapter validates the image.
5. Source registry computes or verifies the source hash.
6. Source is associated with the round.
7. Analysis orchestrator creates a processing attempt.
8. Analysis source association records the exact input hash.
9. Detector produces measurements and observations.
10. Geographic interpretation produces normalized evidence.
11. Scoring engine calculates candidate totals and contributions.
12. Result-state evaluator classifies the outcome.
13. Analysis is stored with a terminal status.
14. Current analysis status is exposed to the user.
15. Explanation is generated only when requested.
16. Explanation request creates a checkpoint.
17. Player guess and actual location are entered separately.
18. Evaluation service creates an immutable evaluation.
19. Review and learning services use the resulting records.
```

## 6.2 Multi-source or multi-frame flow

```text
source A ─┐
source B ─┼─> one AnalysisSource set
source C ─┘
              |
              v
       independent measurements
              |
              v
       source-aware observations
              |
              v
       explicit aggregation rules
              |
              v
       preserved support and conflict evidence
```

The first implementation validates single-image analyses. When multiple sources
are later supported, frames are analyzed independently and source-specific
evidence is preserved when they disagree. Generalized aggregation rules are
deferred until they can be specified and validated; they must be versioned and
must preserve whether a clue appeared repeatedly, only once, or conflicted
across frames.

## 6.3 Explanation and checkpoint flow

```text
latest completed analysis
          |
          v
explanation service
          |
          +--> staged hint response
          |
          +--> full explanation response
                         |
                         v
                 checkpoint service
                         |
                         v
                 immutable checkpoint
```

The UI must identify the analysis ID represented by the explanation.

## 6.4 Evaluation flow

```text
player guess revision
          +
verified actual-location revision
          +
selected analysis/checkpoint
          |
          v
immutable evaluation
          |
          v
round review and current summaries
```

Corrected actual locations create new evaluations rather than mutating the
existing evaluation.

