## 11. Interfaces between components

The initial implementation should define language-level interfaces or typed
contracts around these operations.

## 11.1 Acquisition

```text
acquire(input_reference) -> SourceInput
validate(SourceInput) -> SourceValidationResult
```

`SourceInput` contains source identity and metadata, not geographic meaning.
Its provenance identifies where the input came from and must not be interpreted
as geographic evidence.

## 11. Measurement

```text
measure(source_input, detector_config)
    -> MeasurementSet
```

Measurements identify values, units, regions, and provenance.

## 11. Observation

```text
interpret_measurements(measurements, detector_config)
    -> ObservationSet
```

Observations are visual interpretations, not country rankings.

## 11. Geographic interpretation

```text
interpret_geography(observations, approved_claim_versions)
    -> EvidenceSet
```

The operation must preserve claim provenance and uncertainty.

## 11. Scoring

```text
score(evidence, candidates, scoring_configuration_version)
    -> RankingResult
```

`RankingResult` contains candidate scores, contributions, inclusion status, and
uncertainty classification.

## 11. Explanation

```text
explain(analysis_result, disclosure_level)
    -> Explanation
```

The explanation is derived from the stored result and cannot add unsupported
facts.

## 11. Evaluation

```text
evaluate(prediction, player_guess, actual_location, evaluation_rules)
    -> EvaluationResult
```

Evaluation consumes recorded outcomes and is not part of prediction.

