## 12. Initial implementation architecture

The first implementation should be a local, non-UI vertical slice:

```text
local image file
  -> source validation and hash
  -> one round
  -> analysis attempt
  -> road measurements
  -> normalized road observations
  -> minimal approved geographic claims
  -> candidate scores
  -> score contributions
  -> traceable explanation
```

The first slice does not require live capture, a desktop interface, advanced
machine learning, persistent player-study workflows, or persistent
personalized-insight snapshots. Checkpoints, guesses, actual locations,
evaluations, and regional candidate scoring are target-model features to add
after the local reasoning path is validated.

## 12.1 Recommended initial modules

The existing source layout can evolve toward:

```text
src/
  acquisition/
  analysis/
    measurements/
    observations/
  geography/
  scoring/
  explanation/
  study/
  persistence/
  models/
```

This is a conceptual direction, not a requirement to create all directories at
once.

## 12.2 Existing prototype mapping

| Existing module | Architectural role | Current condition |
|---|---|---|
| `src/main.py` | Temporary orchestration/CLI | Mixes orchestration, paths, output, and labels |
| `src/dataset.py` | Label/ground-truth loading | Minimal CSV loader |
| `src/features/road.py` | Measurement and observation prototype | Returns dictionaries and prints diagnostics |
| `src/detection.py` | Intended detector layer | Mostly stubs and hardcoded test values |
| `src/metas.py` | Intended metadata model | Category container; missing the referenced `GeoMetas` type |
| `src/knowledge.py` | Geographic claim catalog prototype | Partial clue descriptions; not connected to scoring |
| `src/reasoning.py` | Evidence/explanation prototype | Container and helper only |
| `src/scoring.py` | Candidate scoring prototype | Disconnected and expects a different meta representation |

The initial framework should adapt or replace these contracts deliberately. It
should not expand the current inconsistencies into additional layers.

